// PSS v3.0 LRM — Example 199: Degenerate scenario (page 279)
scenario spans.
In the scheduling scenario, the subscenarios are matched from the checkpoint of the scheduling scenario or
after it. The checkpoints of individual subscenarios are independent of each other. The realizations of
scenario schedule { s1,…,sn } consist of member-wise realization unions of subscenarios s1,..., and
sn, provided that these realizations of different scenarios are pairwise disjoint. For example, if set
{a,b} is a realization of s1, set {c} is a realization of s2 and set {d,e,f} is a realization of s3, then set
{a,b,c,d,e,f} is a realization of schedule { s1,s2,s3 }; here, a, b, c, d, e, and f are action executions.
Now consider monitors m defined in Example 200, the action traces shown in Figure 43, and the checkpoint
t0.
c1: cover {
  activity {
    select {
      do a;
      {}
    }
  }
}
c2: cover {
  activity {
    sequence {
      select {
        do a;
        {}
      }
    do b;
  }
}
